WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.380
Since 2000, China's output per
person has risen about 5.6 times.

2
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:12.410
Over the same years, the UK's
index went from 100 to just 122.

3
00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.250
China grew far, far faster.

4
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:18.190
And yet, on average,
people in the UK still

5
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.520
produce much more each.

6
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.990
So if China grew so
much faster than the UK,

7
00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.110
why are its people
still poorer on average?

8
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.940
In this mission, you'll turn
raw figures into index numbers,

9
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.580
and compare Brazil, Russia, India,

10
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.850
China and South Africa since 2000.

11
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:40.150
Then you'll see what their
rise means for the UK:

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.990
new markets, cheaper goods
and tougher competition.

13
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.050
Your mission: find out
what fast growth does,

14
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:48.670
and does not, tell you.
